# Changelog for Xano JavaScript SDK

## 3.1.0
* feature: Support for Realtime v2 via the `realtimeVersion: 2` client setting. Defaults to `1`, so existing apps are unaffected
* feature: Realtime connections reconnect automatically and re-join their channels — on both v1 and v2 — after an abnormal close (deploy, pod restart, network drop)
* feature: On a v2 `at_least_once` channel, messages missed while disconnected are redelivered through the normal `message` handler, marked with `replayed: true`. Cursor acknowledgement is automatic, and waits for `async` handlers to finish
* feature: New `manualAck` channel option and `channel.ack(id)` for apps that acknowledge after their own work (e.g. a database write)
* feature: New `messageType` channel option, naming the v2 channel message a publish routes to
* fix: Top-level frame fields (`id`, `channel`, `type`) are no longer dropped when parsing an incoming realtime frame

## 3.0.1
* feature: Add `realtimeConnectionCanonical`, with backwards-compatible support for `realtimeConnectionHash`

## 3.0.0
* Update Axios to latest to fix potential security vulnerabilities
* Migrate package from Gitlab to Github

## 1.0.0
* feature: Support for all supported Xano request types (GET, POST, PATCH, PUT, HEAD, DELETE)
* feature: Added examples for all use cases
* feature: Added test coverage
